WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.020
It's been a big year for twist endings.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:07.250
So far we've seen heroes turn into villains,
villains turn into allies, secret societies

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:11.530
at work, life-altering decisions, and even
one movie that turned out to partially take

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.780
place in a video game.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.220
These are the biggest plot twists of 2019
so far.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.320
Spoilers ahead.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.280
The marketing for Us presented the film as
a home invasion thriller with a dark secret.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.300
That secret seems to get revealed when Red
explains the nature of the Tethered and why

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.740
she decided to stage an uprising for her people.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.960
It's a twist, of sorts, but it's really more
of an explanation.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.140
"The two were connected.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:38.880
Tethered together."

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.519
Then the real twist arrives at the very end
of the movie, when Adelaide realizes via a

00:00:43.519 --> 00:00:48.449
long-repressed memory that she's actually
the Tethered one, and that Red was her original

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:51.940
self, who she strangled and hid down in the
tunnels so she could attempt to live a normal

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.700
life.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.600
In retrospect it explains so much, but even
if some viewers guessed it from the beginning,

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.240
watching it all build to that moment remains
intensely satisfying.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.800
There are a number of exciting developments
in the much-anticipated and divisive final

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:09.310
season of Game of Thrones which could be considered
important twists.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:13.710
If we're talking about truly massive twists,
though, we have to talk about the Mad Queen,

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.540
and the fall of Daenerys Targaryen.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.530
Though it had been foreshadowed in various
ways throughout the series, Dany's turn from

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:24.189
righteous crusader for the oppressed to full-on
genocidal dragon rider happened so quickly

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:28.060
in the midst of the show's final season that
many fans were caught off guard.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.100
The episode in which she reached a point of
no return, "The Bells," is one of the most

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:36.200
harrowing moments in the entire series, and
some viewers still have their jaws on the

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:36.720
floor.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:42.020
In 2016, M. Night Shyamalan pulled off what
might be the biggest twist of his career with

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:46.820
the surprise reveal that his thriller Split
was actually a secret sequel to his 2000 classic

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:47.620
Unbreakable.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.920
Glass is a follow-up to both films that brings
together the heroes and villains of each story

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.820
into one superhero universe, but it gets even
wilder from there.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.400
It turns out that Kevin Wendell Crumb, a.k.a.
the Horde, and David Dunn, a.k.a.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.960
The Overseer, are not the most powerful forces
in their world.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.080
As their final clash is underway, Shyamalan
reveals that they were brought together not

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:13.230
to be studied or have their superpowers revealed,
but to be executed by a secret society determined

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.680
to keep the balance by wiping out gifted people.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.760
Then, of course, Shyamalan couldn't help but
throw in another twist by making the brilliant

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:24.390
Mr. Glass construct a counter-scheme that
resulted in proof of superheroes being released

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:28.020
to the world, establishing the potential for
an even bigger universe.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.640
And, presumably, even more twists to come.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.740
Avengers: Endgame was only ever going to end
one way: with the Avengers finding a path

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:39.700
to defeating Thanos and restoring their snapped-out
friends to life after the events of Infinity

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:40.420
War.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:41.920
We knew that going in.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.000
The only mystery was in how it would happen,
and the film threw viewers for a loop just

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.560
a few minutes into the adventure.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:52.500
The stage is set for an Avengers vs. Thanos
rematch almost right away, but when the surviving

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:56.670
members of Earth's Mightiest Heroes get to
him, Thanos reveals that he's already destroyed

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:57.840
the Infinity Stones.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.940
"I used the stones to destroy the stones.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.000
It nearly killed me.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.420
But the work is done."

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.620
Thor executes Thanos, and before we can even
get over the shock of that death, the film

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.900
jumps ahead five years to show a seemingly
doomed world.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:19.320
The 2019 film adaptation of Stephen King's
Pet Sematary didn't attempt to hide its major

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.180
alterations to the source material.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.660
Some of the film's earliest trailers gave
away that the new movie was going to make

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:29.180
the Creed family's eldest child, Ellie, the
victim of a tragic early death and even more

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:30.520
tragic resurrection.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:35.180
That runs contrary to King's book, which kills
off the family's youngest child, Gage.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:39.680
It was a big change that seemed to allow the
filmmakers more leeway to play with the psychological

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.420
terror while also upping the violence factor
of the undead child.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:47.200
It was also a brilliant bait and switch hiding
the film's real twist.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:52.140
The original story ends with Louis Creed's
killer undead son murdering his wife, which

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:57.020
then drives Louis to bury her in the cemetery
to bring her back as an undead ghoul as well.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:01.320
In the new film, the undead Ellie kills both
her mother and father and buries them in the

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:06.440
cemetery, and then the trio of undead Creeds
descends on a young Gage as the movie ends.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:10.900
It ups the horror quotient of the film's final
minutes quite a bit, and while not all fans

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.640
will agree with the new direction, there's
little doubt that few of us saw it coming.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:19.480
Serenity came and went as a blip on the screen
in the midst of a crowded year for movies,

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:23.420
despite a cast that includes Oscar winners
Matthew McConaughey and Anne Hathaway.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:27.540
Serenity is the story of a fisherman and boat
captain who's obsessed with catching a big

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.340
tuna that always seems to avoid him.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:33.500
His relatively boring life is changed when
his ex-wife shows up and offers him a ton

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.800
of money to kill her abusive new husband.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:39.200
So far, all the ingredients for a nice little
thriller are there.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.840
And then it turns out this is all happening
inside a video game.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:47.320
That's right, the story of Serenity is actually
that a 13-year-old boy has programmed a video

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:51.300
game as a therapeutic exercise to reconnect
with his dead father.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.680
Then he decides to change the game's programming
when he realizes he wants to kill his abusive

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:56.440
stepfather.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:00.640
Then things get even weirder when the game
itself seems to want to deny its own programming

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.300
and somehow prevent the murder.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:07.060
You'd think the biggest twist in Spider-Man:
Far From Home would come from Mysterio, the

00:05:07.069 --> 00:05:11.099
man who uses super-advanced illusion tech
to trick everyone into thinking he's a superhero

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.160
fighting off city-destroying monsters.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:17.360
The trouble is, a lot of people guessed the
twist that Mysterio was a villain just from

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:21.430
watching the film's trailers and understanding
that Mysterio is traditionally a villain in

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:22.320
the comics.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:26.280
To be truly surprised by a daring twist, you
have to stick around until the mid-credits

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:27.000
scene.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.120
There, it's revealed that Mysterio doctored
a video before his death to make Spider-Man

00:05:31.129 --> 00:05:34.940
look like the true villain of their struggle,
while also outing Peter Parker as the man

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:35.860
in the mask.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:40.560
This sudden change in the character's status
quo, plus the sudden return of J.K. Simmons'

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.930
J. Jonah Jameson to the Spider-Man universe,
is enough to make the audience feel as shocked

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.140
as Peter Parker.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:51.320
Set in 1969 Hollywood, Once Upon a Time in
Hollywood shows us a history of a tipping

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:54.660
point within both the film industry and Los
Angeles as a whole.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:59.060
There's a sense of a city and an art form
on the brink, and Quentin Tarantino successfully

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.630
creates the feeling that anything might happen.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:05.400
Then, as the film reaches its climax, he drops
the big twist.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.879
It turns out that anything-can-happen feeling
is there to set up Tarantino's dream version

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:14.400
of events: a world in which Sharon Tate and
her friends are never murdered by the Manson

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:18.220
Family, and the Family members are instead
fought off by Cliff Booth and Rick Dalton.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:22.920
Sharon survives, Rick gets another shot at
a career, and Cliff is along for the ride.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:27.640
It's a bittersweet happily ever after, and
one that lands even if you do see it coming.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:32.340
There are two major twists in Joker, and both
are presented in a way that creates a certain

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:35.300
sense of ambiguity so that you're not sure
what to believe.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:39.280
The first arrives when it's revealed that
Arthur Fleck might actually be the illegitimate

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:43.180
son of Thomas Wayne himself, which makes him
Bruce Wayne's half brother.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:47.539
Doubt is later cast on this claim, but Arthur
seems to cling to it, and that attachment

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.520
pays off later.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:53.440
The film's ending drops the second major twist:
the riot Arthur Fleck inspired creates the

00:06:53.449 --> 00:06:56.180
environment in which Bruce Wayne's parents
were killed.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:00.920
So, in the continuity of this movie, the Joker
inadvertently creates Batman.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.479
Does this make the film too twisty for its
own good?

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:07.420
Your mileage may vary, but there's no doubt
you left the theater thinking about it.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:12.199
Shazam! seemed to be a pretty traditional
superhero origin story as it follows Billy

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:16.320
Batson and his journey from orphan boy to
impossibly powerful superhero.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:20.580
We see Billy learning to use his new powers
in a mature way, his connection to the people

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:25.050
who become his chosen family, and his eventual
defeat of the supervillain Sivana not just

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:27.160
through brawn, but through the power of love.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:30.260
The twist comes in just how that love manifests
itself.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:34.039
In the midst of his final battle with Sivana,
Billy remembers the wizard who gave him his

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:36.540
powers hinted that he would be able to share
that power.

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:40.040
"With your heart, unlock your greatest power.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:43.980
The thrones of our brothers and sisters await!"

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:48.460
Billy realizes that means that he must pass
his gifts onto his chosen family.

00:07:48.469 --> 00:07:53.529
And that's how, in 2019, we got the Shazam
Family on the big screen.The film's willingness

00:07:53.529 --> 00:07:57.340
to put such a massive new development out
there so late in the story was part of what

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:58.700
made it so much fun.

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:03.760
One of the biggest keys to Parasite's success
is the way it lulls you into thinking everything's

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:07.660
going to go one way before zipping off in
another, unexpected direction.

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:12.279
The major turn comes midway through the film,
just after the Kim family has thoroughly infiltrated

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:13.800
the Park family's lives.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:18.440
At this point, director Bong Joon-Ho has expertly
planted the seeds for what we think is about

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:21.900
to happen, which is the Park family's slow
discovery that the Kim family have conned

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:22.680
them.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:27.420
Then the doorbell rings, and the fired housekeeper
who we never expected to see again shows up.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:32.000
Then she enters the Park house again, and
reveals both the secret bunker beneath the

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.540
structure, and the man living down there.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:38.560
It's a brilliant turn that subverts expectations
and fits perfectly within the film's framework.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:44.000
Knives Out provides ample opportunities for
twists and turns during its runtime, and writer/director

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.820
Rian Johnson delivers plenty.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:50.230
However, the biggest plot twist at work in
Knives Out involves Harlan Thrombey, a noted

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:53.980
mystery writer who's found dead of an apparent
suicide at the beginning of the film.

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:58.260
It's eventually revealed that Harlan did commit
suicide, after his nurse Marta accidentally

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.920
gave him what she believed to be a fatal dose
of morphine.

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:05.180
Harlan killed himself rather than risk Marta
getting arrested for a simple mistake, but

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.400
it turns out there was even more to the story.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:12.160
In the end, private investigator Benoit Blanc
reveals that Harlan's grandson Ransom actually

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:16.640
switched the labels on Harlan's medication
to engineer the morphine overdose, but Marta

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:19.210
gave Harlan the right medication out of instinct.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:23.680
So, the twist in the end is that there's not
a murder of any kind, and that Harlan's death

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.140
really was just a misguided suicide.

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:30.440
If you walk out of The Lighthouse and someone
asks you what the film's about, there's a

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:33.380
good chance you'll have some difficulty answering
that question.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:37.620
Yes, it's the story of two lighthouse keepers
who seem to be slowly losing their grip on

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:41.890
sanity and reality, but if you really dig
into the intricacies of the film, it's a lot

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.520
more complicated than that.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:47.660
That said, there's still a powerful twist
lying in wait near the end of the film.

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:52.490
It comes when the young wickie Ephraim Winslow
reveals that his real name is Thomas Howard,

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:56.340
and that Winslow was an identity he stole
from a man who died in a timber accident that

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:57.240
he didn't stop.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:01.080
This revelation, and the guilt that comes
with it, helps to add tremendous depth and

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.680
emotional weight to the film's powerful climax.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:08.120
Plus, there's the fact that the twist means
that both major characters are named Thomas,

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:12.340
their similarities contrasting against each
other in progressively more violent ways.

